GIVEN `the Insurer's finding of the cause`             IS A STRING
      `the Insurer's finding of the extent`            IS A NUMBER
      `the independent finding of the cause`           IS A STRING
      `the independent finding of the extent`          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A party`
`7 — the party who pays for the independent assessment and the court fees` MEANS
    IF       `the Insurer's finding of the cause`  EQUALS `the independent finding of the cause`
         AND `the Insurer's finding of the extent` EQUALS `the independent finding of the extent`
    THEN `the Policyholder`
    ELSE `the Insurer`

§ `Article 8 — The claim file`

-- "For each case the claim file includes one or more of the following documents." The chapeau
-- does not say which, or who decides; with "other relevant papers (if any)" at the end of 8.2,
-- the file is never complete by any test the rules give. That matters, because the Insurer's
-- deadline to pay runs from a "complete and valid" file (4.2): finding X20.
-- What is encoded is the list of documents the text makes applicable to the facts of a case:
-- the documents the Insurer may ask for. "(nếu có)" (if any) is a fact of the case.
