GIVEN f IS A `The facts the claim file depends on`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A claim document`
`8 — the documents the claim file may include, for` f MEANS
    mapMaybe `if it applies`
        `the documents of Article 8, each with the fact that brings it in`
    WHERE
        `if it applies` d MEANS IF d's snd THEN JUST (d's fst) ELSE NOTHING
        `the documents of Article 8, each with the fact that brings it in` MEANS
            LIST (PAIR OF `notice of the accident and claim, on the Insurer's form`                              , TRUE)
               , (PAIR OF `the certificate or the contract, and other written agreements`                        , TRUE)
               , (PAIR OF `the vehicle registration, and the Driver's licence valid at the time of the loss`     , TRUE)
               , (PAIR OF `papers on a sale, transfer, gift or authorised use of the vehicle`                    , f's `the vehicle was sold, transferred, given or lent under an authority`)
               , (PAIR OF `a valid inspection certificate, or an equivalent paper`                               , NOT f's `the vehicle runs under a temporary permit or is in its first registration`)
               , (PAIR OF `invoices for towing`                                                                  , f's `towing was hired`)
               , (PAIR OF `invoices for repair or replacement outside the Insurer's guarantee network`           , f's `repaired outside the Insurer's guarantee network`)
               , (PAIR OF `papers fixing the value of the property`                                              , f's `a valuation is needed`)
               , (PAIR OF `an authority's record of the theft or disappearance of the vehicle`                   , f's `the whole vehicle was stolen, robbed or disappeared`)
               , (PAIR OF `papers proving the costs of limiting the loss or following the Insurer's instructions`, f's `costs were incurred to limit the loss or on the Insurer's instructions`)
               , (PAIR OF `the record of a settlement or mediation`                                              , f's `there was a mediation`)
               , (PAIR OF `a court judgment or decision in force`                                                , f's `there is a court judgment or decision`)
               , (PAIR OF `papers transferring the claim against the third party to the Insurer`                 , f's `a third party is liable`)
               , (PAIR OF `copies of the police file on the accident`                                            , f's `the police dealt with the accident`)
               , (PAIR OF `papers on the liability of a third party`                                             , f's `a third party is liable`)
               , (PAIR OF `the assessment report the parties agreed`                                             , TRUE)
               , (PAIR OF `other relevant papers`                                                                , f's `there are other relevant papers`)
               , (PAIR OF `the theft or robbery report, confirmed by the police`                                 , f's `the whole vehicle was stolen, robbed or disappeared`)
               , (PAIR OF `the decision to prosecute and investigate`                                            , f's `there is a decision to prosecute`)
               , (PAIR OF `the decision to suspend the investigation or the prosecution`                         , f's `there is a decision to suspend`)
               , (PAIR OF `a police-confirmed declaration of papers lost with the vehicle`                       , f's `papers were lost with the vehicle`)

§ `Article 9 — Double insurance`

-- Double insurance: the Policyholder has contracts with two or more insurers for the same
-- subject, on the same conditions and the same insured event. For the cover that overlaps, the
-- Insurer pays only in the ratio of its sum insured to the total sums insured of all such
-- contracts in force at the time of the loss; for cover that does not overlap, each settles on
-- its own.
-- LAW fork L6: the Law on Insurance Business, Article 49(1) (law text lines 964-968), calls it
-- double insurance only where the total sums insured EXCEED the market value; Article 9 has no
-- such condition, so it shares out a loss the Law would not (finding X22). The encoding follows
-- the rules as written.
